 "coaching_points": [
  "Warm up 2-3 minutes \u2014 light jog, arm circles, wrist rolls, and easy two-hand catches of a soft toss",
  "The wall is a MIRROR \u2014 server throws at an angle from 8m square-on, rebound comes off the OPPOSITE side; keeper sets on that mirror line, 4-5m off the wall and offset 2-3m to the side",
  "This IS reaction work \u2014 a partner's throw hits the wall and the keeper can't predict the exact bounce; the unknown angle and pace is what trains true reactions",
  "Set your feet BEFORE the rebound arrives \u2014 hands ready at hip height, eyes through the ball into the catch",
  "Server varies pace and height every throw \u2014 flat skidders, hip height, head height \u2014 so the keeper reads the bounce late",
  "One ball only: catch clean, throw it straight back to the server \u2014 that return is your reset before the next serve",
  "Target: 8 of 10 rebounds held clean with no spills \u2014 count catches out loud",
  "10 catches per set, 4 sets; swap keeper and server every set \u2014 collecting and returning the ball is the rest",
  "Soft hands on low skidders \u2014 collapse behind the ball, land on forearm and hip, never elbows"
 ],
 "variations": [
  "Low skidders \u2014 server drills the wall flat so rebounds stay under knee height for collapse catches",
  "High hands \u2014 throws at head height for reflex catches above the shoulders",
  "Catch-then-shuffle \u2014 two side steps back to the mirror spot after each hold, then reset for the next serve"
 ],
